# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PRIVATE TREES — this repo is PUBLIC. These must never enter it.
#
# These were previously excluded ONLY by `.git/info/exclude`, which is
# per-clone, untracked, and NOT recreated by `git clone`. A fresh clone
# followed by `git add -A` would therefore have staged the entire private
# business SSoT and the local secrets vault into a public repository.
# Verified 2026-07-26: nothing has ever leaked — every path below is clean
# across the whole history. This is preventive, and it travels with the repo.
# `.git/info/exclude` is intentionally left in place as a second layer.
# [pipeline F-6]
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
knowledge/
company/
# `Private/` existed as an EMPTY, UNIGNORED directory at the repo root until
# 2026-08-15. Git does not track empty directories, so nothing had leaked — but
# the first file placed there would have been staged by `git add -A` into the
# PUBLIC repo, and a directory called `Private` is precisely where somebody puts
# the thing that must not be public. Ignored before it was used, rather than
# after. The case matters on Linux/CI even though Windows would not care.
Private/
private/
# ANCHORED to the repo root on purpose. Without the leading slash this pattern
# matches a directory named `scripts` at ANY depth — it was written for the
# local helper scripts here, and it silently swallowed tooling/scripts/ the
# first time one was added (2026-07-29, S-12's provisioner). `git add <path>`
# warns; `git add -A` would simply have dropped the file, and the loss would
# have surfaced as a missing tool in someone else's clone.
/scripts/
CLAUDE.md

# Personal/ — the OWNER'S OWN documents, not the business's: Form 16, AIS/TIS,
# ITR acknowledgements. These carry PAN, salary figures and date of birth, and
# `origin` is a PUBLIC repository. Added 2026-07-28, before anything in it was
# ever staged (verified: never tracked, never committed, absent from all history).
# Everything under it, at any depth, including the folder's own dotfiles.
Personal/
Personal/**

# Generated git bundles — the code's second offsite copy [pipeline F-7b].
# Regenerated by .claude/scripts/backup-knowledge.ps1 on every run; never
# committed (a repo containing a bundle of itself is a recursion nobody needs).
.bundles/

