apps/subly/config/*.json
!apps/subly/config/*.example.json

# ── Flutter / Dart (GLOBAL — survives app/→apps/ move) ──
**/.dart_tool/
**/.flutter-plugins
**/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
**/build/
**/.packages
**/pubspec.lock
**/ios/Pods/
**/android/.gradle/
**/android/local.properties
**/*/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.*
**/windows/flutter/ephemeral/
**/linux/flutter/ephemeral/
**/macos/Flutter/ephemeral/

# ── Node / Cloudflare / web (GLOBAL) ──
**/node_modules/
# Worker lockfiles ARE tracked (reversed 2026-07-26, [pipeline F-8]).
#
# The previous rule ignored them, reasoning that "the services/* lanes run
# `npm install`, not `npm ci`, so a committed lock buys nothing". That is
# circular — the lock bought nothing *because* nothing used it — and it was
# written before `deploy-workers.yml` existed. The consequence was live: the CI
# dry-run that "proved" a Worker deploy and the deploy itself each ran their own
# `npm install`, minutes apart, against caret ranges. Whichever version won that
# race is what reached production, holding the credential that applies D1
# migrations. `git checkout <sha> && npm install` could never reproduce a
# shipped build.
#
# Both service lockfiles are now committed and every lane uses `npm ci`.
**/.wrangler/
**/dist/
**/_site/
coverage/

# ── COMMITTED generated design tokens (Style Dictionary outputs) — re-include ──
!/packages/tokens/build/
!/packages/tokens/build/**

# ── Pub workspace root artifacts ──
/.dart_tool/
# Root workspace lock IS committed (reproducible app builds; apps/subly is a
# resolution: workspace member). Member locks stay ignored via **/pubspec.lock above.
!/pubspec.lock

# ── IDE / Melos ──
/.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/

# ── OS / editor ──
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# ── Internal planning docs (kept OUT of the public repo) ──
/Backend Research - Firebase vs Cloudflare (July 2026).md
/Subscription tracker app design/
/NIKATRU_GAP_ANALYSIS*.md

# ── strategy docs -> the private nikatru-private repo (was nikatru-company, retired 2026-08-12, ADR 046) ──
/PROJECT_STATE.md
/NIKATRU_MASTER_REQUIREMENTS.md

# Throwaway apps stamped by the brick CI lane (P0.7).
#
# BOTH variants, and the second half was missing until 2026-07-28: the lane
# stamps `_probe_vars.json` (app_id `probe`) AND `_probe_backend_vars.json`
# (app_id `probeapi`), and the backend variant also generates a Worker. Only the
# `probe` names were listed, so stamping the backend variant locally left
# `apps/probeapi/` and `services/probeapi-api/` untracked-but-not-ignored — one
# `git add -A` from committing generated code. Noticed while verifying [2]C-11
# against both stamps; the same class as the documented gotcha where a leftover
# `apps/probe` on disk makes assert-lane-coverage fail locally.
apps/probe/
services/probe-api/
apps/probeapi/
services/probeapi-api/

# Mason local brick cache
.mason/
mason-lock.json

# Flutter platform build outputs (scaffolded 2026-07-25)
**/windows/flutter/ephemeral/
**/linux/flutter/ephemeral/
**/macos/Flutter/ephemeral/

# gen-l10n OUTPUT (2026-08-08, P2.3). `flutter: generate: true` + l10n.yaml
# regenerate these on every `pub get`, and the files ship blanket
# `ignore_for_file: type=lint` headers — assert-no-gate-weakening walks
# `git ls-files` precisely so machine-generated suppressions stay outside its
# domain, which makes UNTRACKED the designed state for them. Factory-wide
# pattern: every stamped app produces the same triplet.
apps/*/lib/l10n/app_localizations*.dart

# …and gen-l10n's DIAGNOSTIC output, which lands in the app root rather than
# beside the generated Dart (2026-08-08, P4 L0). `untranslated-messages-file:` in
# l10n.yaml is resolved relative to the package, so `flutter gen-l10n` and every
# `pub get` drop this file into the tracked tree — measured, not assumed. It is a
# BUILD PRODUCT recomputed from the .arb files on every run, so committing it
# would create a second, staler copy of a fact the .arb files already carry, and
# a reviewer would have no way to tell which one was current. The parity
# assertion lives in `test/l10n_parity_test.dart`, which is tracked and does fail.
apps/*/l10n-untranslated.json
